"time":"2017-08-18T15:00Z","kt":40,"category":0,"pressure_mb":1004,"lat":13.2,"lon":-61.2},{"time":"2017-08-26T03:00Z","kt":115,"category":4,"pressure_mb":937,"lat":28.0,"lon":-96.9},{"time":"2017-08-26T06:00Z","kt":105,"category":3,"pressure_mb":948,"lat":28.2,"lon":-97.1},{"time":"2017-08-30T08:00Z","kt":40,"category":0,"pressure_mb":991,"lat":29.8,"lon":-93.5}],"season":{"ace":224.88,"named":17,"hurricanes":10,"major":6,"ace_rank_since_1950":4,"tna_sst_aso":0.17,"tna_sst_rank_since_1950":14,"n_seasons":76},"notes":[{"text":"Made landfall near Rockport as a Category 4, then stalled over southeast Texas for days. Peak storm total 60.58 in near Nederland \u2014 the wettest tropical cyclone on record in the U.S.","source":"NHC Tropical Cyclone Report AL092017","url":"https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/data/tcr/AL092017_Harvey.pdf"},{"text":"At least 68 direct deaths in Texas, over half in Harris County, almost all from freshwater flooding; about $125 billion in damage, tied with Katrina as the costliest U.S. tropical cyclone.","source":"NHC Tropical Cyclone Report AL092017","url":"https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/data/tcr/AL092017_Harvey.pdf"},{"text":"Climate signal: human-caused warming likely raised Harvey's Houston-area rainfall by at least 19% (best estimate ~38%) and made it at least 3.5\u00d7 more likely.","source":"Risser & Wehner 2017, Geophysical Research Letters","url":"https://escholarship.org/uc/item/0k28z28b"},{"text":"A second, independent study found the record 3-day rainfall over Houston was about 15% more intense and roughly 3\u00d7 more likely than in the early 1900s.","source":"van Oldenborgh et al. 2017 (World Weather Attribution), Environmental Research Letters","url":"https://www.preventionweb.net/news/human-caused-warming-likely-intensified-hurricane-harveys-rains"}],"caveat":"Both studies attribute Harvey's rainfall, not its formation or wind strength."},{"id":"AL022024","name":"Beryl","year":2024,"headline":"Hurricane Beryl \u00b7 Jul 2024","first":"2024-06-2